wb-sway-kiosk for Debian
------------------------

The wb-sway-kiosk package provides a fullscreen HDMI kiosk session for
Wiren Board devices. The systemd unit is wb-sway-kiosk.service, and it runs
Sway on tty1 as root with SWAY_ALLOW_ROOT=1.

Sway starts Squeekboard, the Squeekboard visibility watcher, and Firefox from
/usr/share/wb-sway/sway/config. Before Sway starts, the service snapshots
selected /etc/wb-hardware.conf values into /run/wb-sway-kiosk so all helpers
use the same URL, Firefox mode, volume, and lock directory.

Supported config options are mod4.options.url, mod4.options.ff_mode,
mod4.options.volume, mod4.options.mouse, mod4.options.mode, and
mod4.options.rotate. Use systemctl start, stop, or status with
wb-sway-kiosk.service to control the session.
